    "title_en": "Constant-round quantum advantage in communication complexity for total functions",
    "abstract_en": "We show that there exists a total function for which there is a polynomial gap between the randomized and the constant-round quantum communication complexity. Previously, such a separation was known only for quantum protocols using polynomially many rounds.",
